;; Ground truth for karamazov-ei6t.14 — questions whose answers real runs
;; actually wrote into memory.
;;
;; DERIVED FROM PRESERVED RECORDINGS, not invented. Every :expect below is a
;; substring of a memory that a live arena run wrote by itself, which is what
;; makes this better than a synthetic corpus: a fixture somebody wrote for
;; recall to rank measures how well recall ranks that person's prose.
;;
;; :ask is phrased as a question an implementor would actually ask on a fresh
;; checkout — the situation memory exists for — and deliberately NOT in the
;; memory's own words, or the test measures string equality rather than
;; retrieval.
;;
;; SUBSTRING, not a judge. This scores RETRIEVAL; grading it with a model
;; would fold the model's reading into the number the retrieval is being
;; measured by.

{:subject "endless-flight"
 :source "sweep5 recordings, 2026-09-10"
 :cases
 [{:ask "how do I run the test suite"
   :expect "jolt -M:test"}
  {:ask "how do I take a screenshot of the game"
   :expect "RAYLIB_APP_SHOT"}
  {:ask "how far does the ground get drawn"
   :expect "terrain-half"}
  {:ask "where do I register a new test namespace"
   :expect "test_runner"}
  {:ask "what do I have to call before eval"
   :expect "plan"}
  {:ask "where do colours come from"
   :expect "palette"}]}
